  "preamble": "Devoicing of the bilabial implosive to [p], here in two steps. In Khmer, Proto-Austroasiatic *ɓ appears as Old Khmer b (ពិរ៑ bir 'two'), and Old Khmer voiced stops later lost their voicing, leaving the old voicing contrast as vowel register (the o-series): Modern Khmer ពីរ /piː/, ពុល /pul/, ពាក់ /pĕəʔ/. The Pearic languages Chong and Pear also have p for *ɓ. Modern Khmer ɓ and ɗ are secondary, from earlier *p and *t (បី 'three' < Old Khmer ⟨pi⟩ [ɓiː] < *peːʔ; ដៃ 'hand' < *t₁iiʔ), so the two series swapped places.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Devoicing, Loss of Implosion, Airstream Change",
